Conclusion
----------

Monterey removes the modern-HWX compatibility blocker for staged fp16 projections.
The 3.5 GiB Linux ANE DART VM cannot hold the full fp16 model at once.
The runtime must stream bounded projection programs and preserve recurrent state separately.
Full-model Linux token parity and both performance targets remain open.
